PHASE 1: DATA MODEL + AUTHORIZATION (2-4 days)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Backend Changes
- Add organizations table:
  - id, name, status (active|on_hold|deactivated), primary_user_id (nullable), timestamps.
- Add organization_user (membership) table:
  - id, organization_id, user_id, role_id, status (invited|active|suspended), invited_at, accepted_at, timestamps, soft delete (if chosen).
- Add roles + role_permissions model for extensible role templates:
  - roles: id, scope (platform|organization), key, name, description, is_system, is_active, created_by, timestamps.
  - role_permissions: id, role_id, permission_key, timestamps.
- Add/enable soft deletes:
  - users (if approved), angles, angle_templates, user_api_instances, user_api_instance_values,
    thank_you_pages, otp credentials/pixels tables as finalized in cascade matrix.
- Add organization_id to high-traffic domain tables (preferred) OR enforce via membership joins.

Indexes
- organization_id on org-scoped entities.
- (organization_id, user_id) unique on membership.
- deleted_at composite indexes for filtered lists.
- role_id index on membership; unique (scope, key) on roles.

Authorization
- Add policy/gate layer for org roles:
  - view/edit own assigned assets.
  - org-wide visibility for Admin/Manager as approved.
  - cross-org operations restricted to Super Admin only.
- Add role guardrails:
  - org users cannot create/update/archive roles.
  - archive role instead of delete when role is in use.
  - prevent role assignment escalation outside actor permissions.

Small steps
- Step 1.1 [DONE]: Create migrations for organizations + membership.
- Step 1.2 [DONE]: Add roles/role_permissions tables and seed base roles.
- Step 1.3 [DONE]: Add organization_id columns (or join strategy) to scoped resources.
